{"entries":[{"caption":"Seasonal course of GPP (black lines) and vegetation indices (NDVI, CCI, NIRv, and kNDVI) before (blue points) and after (red points) snow removal (“SR”). Data were collected from the CA-Qfo flux site in 2009. Grey-shaded areas denote snow-affected periods, and the vertical yellow band indicates snow-melt period in the late spring based on visual inspection of PhenoCam imagery. We also identified an additional snow day on October 13, 2009 using PhenoCam imagery.","key":"fig-snowonVI","order":{"number":3,"section":[0,3,0,0,0,0,0]}},{"caption":"Seasonal patterns of photosynthetic rate and leaf-­ level vegetation indices for evergreen (a, c, e, and g) and deciduous (b, d, f, and h) species. The period of new-­ leaf expansion (E) is labeled in panel (a).","key":"fig-timeleafdata","order":{"number":2,"section":[0,2,0,0,0,0,0]}},{"caption":"See the unseen through the hyperspectral and thermal lens from the air.","key":"fig-ImageAnalysis","order":{"number":6,"section":[0,6,0,0,0,0,0]}},{"caption":"Scale dependence of remote sensing of biodiversity. Sampling at coarser scales leads to information loss seen as decreased spectral variation and, as a consequence, decreases the accuracy of biodiversity estimation through spectral diversity.","key":"fig-scalebiodiversity","order":{"number":1,"section":[0,1,0,0,0,0,0]}},{"caption":"Hypothetical (left) and empirical (right) PRI and SIF light responses between functional types and at different seasons (decreasing photosynthesis, decreasing SIF, and decreasing xanthophyll cycle activity during senescence). Irradiance, PRI and SIF were derived directly from the airborne imagery.","key":"fig-urbantreehealth","order":{"number":5,"section":[0,5,0,0,0,0,0]}},{"caption":"Testing impacts of management practices using a prairie restoration experiment. Effects of seeding treatments (control, mid- and high-diversity) and managements (burning and haying) on percent cover of vegetation (a), litter (b) and bare soil (c), and functional groups, including C3 grasses (d), and C4 grasses (e), species richness per square meter (f), and remote sensing indicators including NDVI (g), albedo (h), and surface temperature (i).","key":"fig-bobcatresults","order":{"number":4,"section":[0,4,0,0,0,0,0]}}],"headings":["biodiversity","physiology","productivity","environmental-change","urban-ecosystem","rs-method"]}